#### Q20: Design a complete compliance and audit system for sensitive operations.

**Answer:**

**Comprehensive Audit & Compliance Framework:**

```
Audit System Architecture:

┌─────────────────────────────────────────┐
│        Compliance Requirements          │
│   (GDPR, HIPAA, SOX, PCI-DSS)          │
└────────────┬────────────────────────────┘
             ↓
┌─────────────────────────────────────────┐
│      Access Control & Authentication    │
│   - Multi-factor authentication         │
│   - Role-based access control           │
│   - Single sign-on (SSO)                │
└────────────┬────────────────────────────┘
             ↓
┌─────────────────────────────────────────┐
│         Audit Trail Capture             │
│   - Who, What, When, Where, Why         │
│   - Immutable log                       │
│   - Real-time recording                 │
└────────────┬────────────────────────────┘
             ↓
┌─────────────────────────────────────────┐
│      Data Encryption & Protection       │
│   - Encryption at rest                  │
│   - Encryption in transit               │
│   - Key management                      │
└────────────┬────────────────────────────┘
             ↓
┌─────────────────────────────────────────┐
│        Monitoring & Alerting            │
│   - Real-time threat detection          │
│   - Anomaly detection                   │
│   - Alert on suspicious activity        │
└────────────┬────────────────────────────┘
             ↓
┌─────────────────────────────────────────┐
│      Reporting & Investigation          │
│   - Generate compliance reports         │
│   - Investigate incidents               │
│   - Export for regulatory review        │
└─────────────────────────────────────────┘

Implementation:

1. Audit Log Record Type

CREATE AuditLog Record:
├─ auditLogID (Primary key)
├─ timestamp (DateTime) - When
├─ userId (User) - Who
├─ action (Text) - What
│  Values: Create, Read, Update, Delete
├─ entity (Text) - What was changed
│  Values: Customer, Invoice, Employee
├─ entityID (Text) - Which record
├─ oldValue (Text) - Previous value
├─ newValue (Text) - New value
├─ reason (Text) - Why (from user)
├─ ipAddress (Text) - Where
├─ sessionID (Text) - Tracking
├─ status (Text) - Success/Failure
└─ details (Text) - Additional info

2. Automatic Logging Mechanism

On Record Update:
[Record Updated]
  ├─ [Service Task] Log to AuditLog
  └─ Create entry:
     {
       timestamp: now(),
       userId: user.id,
       action: "UPDATE",
       entity: "Invoice",
       entityID: ri!invoice.id,
       oldValue: ri!oldInvoice.amount,
       newValue: ri!invoice.amount,
       reason: ri!changeReason
     }

3. Sensitive Data Masking

For Display:
- Credit Card: Show last 4 digits only
- SSN: Show last 4 digits only
- Password: Never display
- PHI: Encrypt if displayed

SAIL Example:
a!textDisplayField(
  label: "Social Security",
  value: "***-**-" & right(ri!ssn, 4)
)

4. Access Control

Role-Based Access:
├─ Viewer: Read-only access
├─ Editor: Create/Edit
├─ Approver: Approve/Reject
├─ Admin: Full access
└─ Auditor: Read audit logs

Field-Level Security:
├─ Public fields: All roles
├─ Internal fields: Staff only
├─ Confidential: Executives only
└─ Restricted: Admin only

5. Compliance Reporting

Monthly Compliance Report:
├─ Total users
├─ Total auditable transactions
├─ Failed access attempts
├─ Data changes by category
├─ Sensitive field access
├─ Exceptions and overrides
├─ Compliance violations (if any)

Annual Audit Report:
├─ Activity summary
├─ Access patterns
├─ Incident history
├─ Remediation actions
├─ Certification statement

6. Incident Detection

Suspicious Activity Triggers:
├─ Multiple failed logins (> 5)
│  → Lock account, notify admin
├─ Bulk data export
│  → Alert approver
├─ Unauthorized field access
│  → Log and flag
├─ Off-hours access
│  → Notify security team
├─ Sensitive data modification
│  → Require approval
└─ Config changes
   → Admin review required

Example Rule:
RULE_DetectSuspiciousActivity
if(
  failedLoginCount > 5 ||
  bulkExportSize > 10000 ||
  accessTime NOT IN businessHours ||
  user.role != "Admin" && accessing("salary"),
  ALERT_SECURITY_TEAM()
)

7. Data Retention

Retention Policy:
├─ Active records: Indefinite
├─ Archived records: 7 years
├─ Audit logs: 7 years
├─ Deleted records: 90 days (recovery)
├─ Logs older than 7 years: Archive/Destroy

Auto-Archive Job (Monthly):
├─ Identify old records
├─ Move to archive storage
├─ Reduce main database size
├─ Maintain audit trail

8. Multi-Factor Authentication

Login Process:
1. Username/Password
2. OTP via email/SMS
3. Biometric (optional)
4. Session management
5. Timeout after inactivity

9. Encryption Strategy

At Rest:
- Database encryption (AES-256)
- File encryption
- Key management system

In Transit:
- HTTPS/TLS 1.2+
- Certificate pinning
- VPN for sensitive data

10. Compliance Dashboard

Real-time Monitoring:
┌─────────────────────────┐
│ Users Active: 245/250   │
│ Failed Logins: 2        │
│ Audit Logs: 12,500      │
│ Compliance: 99.8%       │
│ Last Backup: 2hrs ago   │
│ Alerts: 0 Critical      │
└─────────────────────────┘
